9 1 "// writeInterruptible is os.write's write to a blocking pipe, as write(2) is under CPython's handlers (no SA_RESTART: a"] [160 1 "// signal interrupts it, os.write's PyErr_CheckSignals runs the handlers, PEP 475's retry; py-mods-1122, test_io's"] [161 1 "// SignalsTest.test_interrupted_write_*, which hung): in the main thread, a FIFO's write (a regular file's never blocks;"] [162 1 "// sockets write by socket's own calls) waits for room by ppoll with the wake pipe (the GIL released, the handlers run when"] [163 1 "// a signal arrives) and writes at most PIPE_BUF bytes at a time, which a pipe that polls writable takes without blocking"] [164 1 "// (no flag of the shared file description changed), until every byte is written; a handler that raises ends it with its"] [165 1 "// exception (CPython's partial count, then the handler's exception at the next check), one that returns lets it go on."] [166 1 "// handled false: not such a write (another thread, a non-blocking descriptor, no FIFO, nothing to write), written as"] [167 1 "// before."] [180 23 "// PIPE_BUF: a pipe that polls writable has at least this much room"]] :go/pos {:name [3 9] :package [3 1]} :go/semis [[97 40] [103 39] [115 33] [127 48] [133 35] [149 91] [152 12] [152 22] [185 35]]} (go/file "builtins_signal_wait.go" :build ["//go:build linux"] :imports [


